{
  "id": 9,
  "title": "Body & health",
  "goal": "Name parts of the body, say what's wrong when you're ill, and understand a doctor's advice.",
  "intro": "When you're unwell in Kerala you'll find a pharmacy (മെഡിക്കൽ ഷോപ്പ്) on almost every street and excellent hospitals in every town. This unit gives you the words to explain your symptoms.\n\nIllness, like liking and wanting, happens **to** you, so Malayalam uses the **dative subject** again: എനിക്ക് പനിയുണ്ട് 'to me there is fever' = 'I have a fever'. You'll also learn **-അണം** 'should / must' — the doctor's favourite ending.",
